From 04770974e7d1cc0810b8c23d8256dd2ea85ef93a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Trung=20L=C3=AA?= <8@tle.id.au>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:21:37 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] Keep BytecodeEmitter::emitTree a thin dispatcher under
 LTO and PGO

emitTree is the recursion point of the bytecode emitter and is written to
use little stack itself, dispatching to one helper per node kind. With
ThinLTO and PGO, clang inlines most of those helpers into it, so its frame
grows from 160 to about 1200 bytes on ppc64le and deeply nested code hits
the native stack limit at less than half the nesting depth a GCC build
handles (environments/bug1966196.js fails in the shell). Mark the large
helpers that emitTree still calls directly MOZ_NEVER_INLINE, as emitSwitch,
emitTry and emitLexicalScope already are for llvm.org/pr14047.
---
 js/src/frontend/BytecodeEmitter.cpp | 138 +++++++++++++++------------
 js/src/frontend/BytecodeEmitter.h   | 139 ++++++++++++++++------------
 2 files changed, 158 insertions(+), 119 deletions(-)

